{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsub", "label": "DistributedPubSub", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The cluster-wide counterpart of the local event stream, keyed on string topics instead of classes; each node hosts a mediator and publishing costs one envelope per node rather than per subscriber.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsubmediator", "label": "DistributedPubSubMediator", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Lives at a well-known path, fans out to local subscribers directly and to each remote node once, giving at-most-one-remote-hop delivery; it watches every local subscriber so a crash without Unsubscribe still removes it when Terminated lands.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_subscribe", "label": "Subscribe", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Its optional third argument names where the acknowledgment or refusal goes; without it the answer follows context.sender, which is empty when mediator.tell is called from outside an actor.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_publish", "label": "Publish", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_subscriberejected", "label": "SubscribeRejected", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A Subscribe over a cap is refused, not dropped: the reply carries which cap refused it and the value that cap is set to.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_anycast", "label": "Anycast one-subscriber delivery", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A rotation, not a draw - ten tasks over three workers land 4/3/3 - with a stable candidate order (locals in registration order, then remote claimants by address). Remote nodes count as one candidate each because the gossip frame carries topic names and not subscriber counts, and a node that both publishes and hosts workers rotates on two cursors so one shared cursor cannot starve the remote candidates. An anycast that crossed a hop and found nobody is not re-routed, because a second hop would trade the at-most-one-hop guarantee for a race against the correcting gossip round.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_topic_gossip", "label": "Topic-to-node gossip deltas", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The mediator keeps its subscriber map local and gossips only 'node X now has/no longer has subscribers for topic Y'; lower intervals converge faster after subscribe/unsubscribe at the cost of more chatter, and the lag is why a publish on another node right after Subscribe can miss.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_bounded_registries", "label": "Bounded mediator registries", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "maxSubscribersPerTopic, maxTopics and maxRemoteNodesPerTopic bound the three things publish fan-out walks. The caps apply to gossip too, which is the half worth knowing: a peer announcing 100 000 topics used to allocate 100 000 entries on every receiving node with no local Subscribe involved. Over-cap claims are dropped and logged while the connection stays up, because one noisy peer should not cost a healthy link.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_dead_letters_unrouted", "label": "Unrouted publishes go to dead letters", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "On by default because a mistyped topic and a topic whose subscribers have not gossiped in yet look identical from the publisher's side, and this is what tells them apart; a frame the mediator has no handler for lands there too, since a silently dropped frame during a rolling upgrade looks exactly like a cluster with nothing to do.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsub", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsubmediator", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsubmediator", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_subscribe", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsubmediator", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_publish", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_subscribe", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_subscriberejected", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_anycast", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_publish", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_bounded_registries", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_distributedpubsubmediator", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_bounded_registries", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_subscriberejected", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_bounded_registries", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_topic_gossip", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_topic_gossip", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_gossip", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/pubsub.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsub_anycast", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_pubsu